Z||000009||Gokart||06-25-2000||06:21 AM||||Does Pisa still make them Rob? How do they fit and was there alot of prep work involved before painting?||||reg||5
Z||000010||Robert||06-25-2000||09:21 AM||||The fit is ok, but you have to drill your own mounting holes. As far as prep goes, there is a lot to be desired.  They come with a gray primer, but still need sanding, filling, sanding, filling and more sanding.  Could take up to 16 hours to smooth them out.  I think the end result is worth it. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Thunder_Nights.JPG">  <P>I don’t know if PISA still sells them or not, here is their web site, give them a call.  I have a copy of their 1999 “BIG Fiero Parts book”, nice book to have, full of great ideas. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html</A> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 06-25-2000).]||||reg||1
